      "note": "Private Act constituting Belfast Rural District, with altered boundaries, as Newtownabbey Urban District and transferring the rest of Belfast RD to Antrim, Lisburn and Larne RDs (objects of the Bill as published in Belfast Gazette issue 1848, 23 Nov 1956, pages 311-312). Royal Assent notified in Belfast Gazette issue 1884, 2 Aug 1957, page 211. Belfast Rural District was abolished and Newtownabbey Urban District formed on 1 Apr 1958: the Newtownabbey Urban District (Electoral Areas) Order (Northern Ireland) 1957 (S.R. & O. 1957 No. 222, https://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisro/1957/222/contents/made) recites that date from the Act, and the Census of Population 1961, General Report (HMSO Belfast), pp. xvi-xvii, changes in administrative areas during the intercensal period, https://www.nisra.gov.uk/publications/1961-census-reports, gives the same day."
